The contract is vulnerable to re-entrancy attack in the following function:

function transferReward(address _to, uint256 _value) {
    require(!frozen[msg.sender]);    
    if (msg.sender.balance  < minBalanceForAccounts) {
        sell((minBalanceForAccounts - msg.sender.balance) * sellPrice);
    }
    totalLockedRewardsOf[msg.sender] -= _value;                           
    lockedRewardsOf[msg.sender][_to] -= _value;
    balanceOf[_to] += _value;
    Unlock(msg.sender, _to, _value);
}

The function above has a Re-Entrancy vulnerability. The logic of the function is that it will unlock rewards for a user, but it will not check the balance of the contract after the unlock operation. This can be exploited by an attacker by calling the transferReward function in a loop, which will empty the contract. More scrutinize this part of the code.

